  "run_id": "23b15d9dc2",
  "final_message": "I reproduced the bug. A slot template whose name starts with an underscore (`#_duration`) is dropped, and the child's fallback content renders instead. This only happens when the parent component also has a conditional slot template (`<template v-if ... #randomslotname>`) next to the child.\n\nThe reproduction is a new test, `packages/vue/__tests__/slotUnderscoreRepro.spec.ts`. It rebuilds the playground from the report with the runtime compiler: `BaseLayout`, `SubComponent` with `title` and `_duration` slots, and an `App` that nests them. Run it from the repo root with:\n\n    npx vitest run --project unit packages/vue/__tests__/slotUnderscoreRepro.spec.ts\n\nThree variants run, and the output of each is logged:\n\n| Variant | Rendered HTML | Result |\n|---|---|---|\n| No conditional sibling template | `<div><b>title works</b><b>_duration works</b></div>` | works |\n| Conditional sibling, slot renamed to `duration` | `<div><p>rand</p><b>title works</b><b>duration works</b></div>` | works |\n| Conditional sibling, slot named `_duration` | `<div><p>rand</p><b>title works</b><span>DEFAULT _duration</span></div>` | bug, test fails |\n\nThe test file also logs the compiled render function. The parent's slots object gets `_: 2 /* DYNAMIC */` because of the `v-if` template, and `BaseLayout` is created with the `DYNAMIC_SLOTS` patch flag.\n\nI haven't checked this against 3.5.13 or 3.5.17, only the checked-out revision.\n\nI also temporarily logged inside `assignSlots` in `packages/runtime-core/src/componentSlots.ts`, then reverted it, so only the new test file is left in the tree. The logs suggest a cause, which I haven't confirmed with a fix:\n\n- In the bug case, `SubComponent`'s slots go through `assignSlots` with `optimized = false`. That is the call with keys `['title', '_duration', '_']`.\n- In the working no-sibling case, `optimized` is `true`.\n- With `optimized = false`, `assignSlots` copies a key only if `!isInternalKey(key)`. `isInternalKey` is `key[0] === '_' || key === '$stable'`, so it also filters out a real slot named `_duration`, not just the compiler's `_` marker.\n- The conditional sibling makes `BaseLayout`'s default slot render with `optimized = false`. This is my reading of the code, not something I traced. With dynamic slots, `renderSlot` produces a BAIL fragment, so `SubComponent` is mounted un-optimized.\n",
  "run_command": "npx vitest run --project unit packages/vue/__tests__/slotUnderscoreRepro.spec.ts",
  "patch": "diff --git a/packages/vue/__tests__/slotUnderscoreRepro.spec.ts b/packages/vue/__tests__/slotUnderscoreRepro.spec.ts\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..12a769c\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/packages/vue/__tests__/slotUnderscoreRepro.spec.ts\n@@ -0,0 +1,90 @@\n+import { compile } from '@vue/compiler-dom'\n+import { createApp } from '../src'\n+\n+// Reproduction for: slot <template> not working when its name starts with an\n+// underscore (_) and the component is a sibling of a conditionally rendered\n+// slot template of the parent component.\n+describe('slot names starting with underscore (repro)', () => {\n+  const BaseLayout = {\n+    template: `<div><slot name=\"randomslotname\"></slot><slot></slot></div>`,\n+  }\n+  const SubComponent = {\n+    template: `<slot name=\"title\"><span>DEFAULT title</span></slot><slot name=\"_duration\"><span>DEFAULT _duration</span></slot>`,\n+  }\n+\n+  function run(appTemplate: string) {\n+    const container = document.createElement('div')\n+    const App = {\n+      components: { BaseLayout, SubComponent },\n+      template: appTemplate,\n+      data: () => ({ cond: true }),\n+    }\n+    createApp(App).mount(container)\n+    return container.innerHTML\n+  }\n+\n+  it('prints compiled output (debug)', () => {\n+    const { code } = compile(\n+      `<BaseLayout>\n+        <template v-if=\"cond\" #randomslotname><p>rand</p></template>\n+        <SubComponent>\n+          <template #title><b>title works</b></template>\n+          <template #_duration><b>_duration works</b></template>\n+        </SubComponent>\n+      </BaseLayout>`,\n+      { mode: 'function' },\n+    )\n+    console.log(code)\n+  })\n+\n+  it('without conditional sibling template (works)', () => {\n+    const html = run(`\n+      <BaseLayout>\n+        <SubComponent>\n+          <template #title><b>title works</b></template>\n+          <template #_duration><b>_duration works</b></template>\n+        </SubComponent>\n+      </BaseLayout>`)\n+    console.log('NO v-if sibling   =>', html)\n+    expect(html).toContain('title works')\n+    expect(html).toContain('_duration works')\n+    expect(html).not.toContain('DEFAULT')\n+  })\n+\n+  it('control: non-underscore name with conditional sibling template (works)', () => {\n+    const container = document.createElement('div')\n+    const Sub = {\n+      template: `<slot name=\"title\"><span>DEFAULT title</span></slot><slot name=\"duration\"><span>DEFAULT duration</span></slot>`,\n+    }\n+    createApp({\n+      components: { BaseLayout, Sub },\n+      data: () => ({ cond: true }),\n+      template: `\n+      <BaseLayout>\n+        <template v-if=\"cond\" #randomslotname><p>rand</p></template>\n+        <Sub>\n+          <template #title><b>title works</b></template>\n+          <template #duration><b>duration works</b></template>\n+        </Sub>\n+      </BaseLayout>`,\n+    }).mount(container)\n+    console.log('CONTROL (no underscore) =>', container.innerHTML)\n+    expect(container.innerHTML).toContain('duration works')\n+    expect(container.innerHTML).not.toContain('DEFAULT')\n+  })\n+\n+  it('with conditional sibling template (BUG)', () => {\n+    const html = run(`\n+      <BaseLayout>\n+        <template v-if=\"cond\" #randomslotname><p>rand</p></template>\n+        <SubComponent>\n+          <template #title><b>title works</b></template>\n+          <template #_duration><b>_duration works</b></template>\n+        </SubComponent>\n+      </BaseLayout>`)\n+    console.log('WITH v-if sibling =>', html)\n+    expect(html).toContain('title works')\n+    expect(html).toContain('_duration works')\n+    expect(html).not.toContain('DEFAULT')\n+  })\n+})\n"
}
